	)
	(text "J11 keeps the original CPU board connector (IO board J16 harness): +5 V, ground and +12 V (pin 6, unregulated); -12 V (pin 3) is not used.\nThe +12 V rail (audio amplifiers, Pi buck) comes from J23 (external, priority) or J11 pin 6 through ideal diodes U33 / U34 (they block reverse polarity), then F1 (4 A hold) and the D5 clamp.\nU3 NCP1117 (as in the RP2350 hardware guide) is stable with ceramic capacitors. All regulator capacitors are 0805 or larger for low DC-bias derating.\nExternal +5 V on J17 has priority: U1 TPS2117 (2:1 mux, 4 A) takes VIN1 while R1 / R2 hold PR1 above 1 V (VIN1 above about 4 V), else J11 on VIN2.\nThe TPS2117 replaces the TPS2121 of ARCHITECTURE.md 9.3 (JLCPCB stock); the KiCad TPS2116DRL symbol has the same pinout.\nJP1 (bridged by default) disconnects the J11 +5 V completely; leaving J17 unplugged forces J11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bde62702-015c-5283-acf0-2bdd4e0c270f")
	)
	(text "IO board power (J11: +5 V, +12 V on pin 6)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
